n the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Sentences", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A simple sentence is a sentence with a subject and a verb. Sometimes it will also have an object.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sally went to the movies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A simple sentence:<br />   <ul><li>is  made from a group of words that express an idea   </li> <li> always starts with a capital letter and finishes with a period (.)</li>  <li>can be very short or very long</li> <li>always has a subject and a verb</li> <li> the subject goes in front of the verb</li> <li>can have more one noun or more as the subject and can also have adjectives, adverbs, and prepositions which give more information </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br>      Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.   </br>   Irregular verbs change in different ways.  </br>  </br>  For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary did followed by      the verb in the base form, like Did you ask \u2026 ? </br>     Did is the past form of to do. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I just purchased my ticket.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I went to the airport.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to surf", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stand on a board and ride the waves in the ocean  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to learn how to surf.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you are going on a trip.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "turtle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an animal with a hard shell on its back", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally wants to swim with the turtles.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to purchase ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to buy ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally purchased her plane ticket on Saturday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "term ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a period of time during the school year ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter wants to finish term one so he can go on holiday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep in touch ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stay in contact with a person or people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to keep in touch when I am traveling.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a famous avenue in Paris ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's walk down the Champs-\u00c9lys\u00e9es.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le08ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The \"ur\" sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If a vowel is followed by an r, the sound of the vowel changes.  This vowel sound is called an r-controlled vowel. </br>The \"er\", \"ir\", and \"ur\" combinations make the same er sound.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " </br>The r-controlled vowel can be spelled 4 different ways.</br>For example: <br>ur as in <span class=\"italic\">burger</span><br> ir as in <span class=\"italic\">first</span><br>  ear as in <span class=\"italic\">earth</span><br> er as in <span class=\"italic\">person</span>  ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose a country you want to visit.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Make a list of 5 attractions you want to visit or activities you want to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 sentences about the attractions or activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use three of these words: <span class=\"italic\">turn</span>, <span class=\"italic\">purchase</span>, <span class=\"italic\">surf</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Saturday</span>, <span class=\"italic\">church</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I use words with the <span class=\"italic\">ur</span> sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose 5 attractions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences about attractions or activities.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say and use the controlled <span class=\"italic\">ur</span> sound. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say simple sentences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify key information in a short audio.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Which p